  "notes": [
    "No sagittal/transverse hyperparameter overrides. Dataset paths and the number/order of landmarks must still match the dataset.",
    "CNN standardisation statistics are calculated from each training split, saved and reused for inference; do not hard-code statistics from an example fold.",
    "The tested ViT pipeline uses per-image min-max scaling, enforce_greyscale=true and normalise_inputs=false.",
    "For pretrained models, freeze_encoder_epochs=5 is the minimum decoder-only duration, not an automatic switch at epoch 5. Transition follows 10 plateau epochs without at least 0.1 px improvement; the best pixel checkpoint is restored.",
    "At the ViT transition the optimiser state is cleared, decoder LR is reset to 0.00005 and encoder LR to 0.00001; the scheduler is restarted.",
    "Plateau scheduling monitors validation pixel error; early stopping monitors validation loss. Select final validation checkpoints by pixel error for consistency with the report.",
    "300 epochs is a ceiling. Do not turn fold_all training-set scores into independent validation evidence.",
    "The saved experiments have geometric weights 0.01 but landmark_constraint_loss=null in normal-loss runs. Zero weights here explicitly reinforce that geometry is disabled; they are inactive when the selector is null.",
